WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.235
-Our next guest stars
alongside John Cena

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:05.104
in the new hit film
"Vacation Friends,"

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.173
which is streaming now on Hulu.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.442
Please welcome Meredith Hagner.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.111
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.846
-♪ Meredith Hagner ♪

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.914
♪ You cannot pretend ♪

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.649
♪ Things just might get freaky ♪

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.118
♪ With "Vacation Friends" ♪

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:20.954
♪ Meredith Hagner ♪

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.356
♪ I know that she could ♪

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:28.627
♪♪

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:30.530
-Yeah!
-Yeah! Hey!

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.131
-Ahh!
-You're here!

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.066
-I keep wanting to give also
my attention to The Roots!

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.335
-Of course.
The Roots right there.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.970
-You guys are so awesome.
-Yeah, you have to.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.239
-Hi, Jimmy.
-Meredith, I'm so happy

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.307
that you're here on the show.
You look gorgeous.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.808
Thank you for coming
to the show.

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:43.843
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.644
-This is your first time
on the show,

00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:47.980
but apparently
we've -- we've met before.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.816
-Yeah, it was really huge
for, I think, both of us.

00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:53.786
No, I --
I met you when I was 16.

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:57.190
-Uh-huh.
-And I was a huge Strokes fan.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.326
Like, arguably the biggest
Strokes fan in the world.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.862
And my dad dropped me off
at the Ritz Theater.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.932
I went by myself to a show
when I was 16.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.968
So it was like 1942,
somewhere around there.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.571
And you opened for The Strokes.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.806
-That's right.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.908
-I opened --
Did you know who I was?

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.577
-Yeah.
-Okay, all right.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.311
-I was a huge fan.
No, you were really funny.

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:20.680
And I was like,
"Who's this guy?"

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.283
I have a photo of you
in a white track suit.

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:27.086
-Yeah, I used to wear white
Juicy Couture track suits.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.188
-Which I was --
I was really into.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.523
And then, I was like --
I got my little T-shirt,

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:34.494
and I was waiting by the,
you know, area in the back --

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.795
What is it? The --
-Yeah, backstage.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.129
-Backstage.

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:40.366
And -- And I was waiting
for the band to sign it,

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.435
and I had my T-shirt out,
and you came up and signed

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.137
my shirt,
which was really nice.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.704
-Oh. See?
-And so people would be like,

00:01:45.704 --> 00:01:47.239
"Oh, did The Strokes
sign your shirt?"

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:49.142
'Cause I wore it, like,
every day of high school.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:53.379
And I'd be like,
"No, the guy that opened did."

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.514
-Yeah, the guy who --
I don't remember his name.

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:56.715
Jerry Falcon."

00:01:56.715 --> 00:01:58.751
-Yeah. "Jerry Falcon did."

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.920
But then, so many people
asked me who it was,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.355
and I had to say "Jimmy Fallon."

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:04.457
So I think I'm really
responsible for your career.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.759
-Wow. Yeah, you -- Thank you.
I appreciate that.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.727
-Enough people
in North Carolina heard,

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:10.729
and now you're here.
-North Carolina. The Ritz.

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:12.665
That's what I'm talking about.
I shall return.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.301
I do remember opening up
for The Strokes.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.537
We opened up for them
for six shows.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:19.973
And I just did --
We had, like, comedy music.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.075
And I was so excited, because
I love The Strokes, as well.

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.343
-Yeah.
-And no one wanted to see me.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.445
No one wants to see a comedian
open up for a band.

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:28.414
-I mean, it's a tough one,
'cause people do go

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.717
for music, specifically,
so you're already starting --

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.852
-We did some gigs where people
would just scream,

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:35.020
"Get off the stage!"

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.990
And I was like, "So, you guys
go to the movie theaters?"

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.392
Just doing my stand-up
or whatever.

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:43.428
I'm so happy, though, that you
saw that and had a good memory.

00:02:43.428 --> 00:02:44.697
-A really good memory.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.265
-Thank you
for coming on the show.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.067
I want to talk about --
There's so many things --

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.935
I want to talk about
your hit Hulu movie.

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:52.238
But, also, you and your husband
just recently had a baby boy.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.907
-Yeah, we did.
-Congratulations.

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.775
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thanks. Thanks.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.677
-And we love Wyatt.
I love Wyatt Russell.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.845
I love him.
Please give him my best.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.947
How old is the baby?
What is the baby's name?

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:03.382
What's he like?
-He's amazing.

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:04.584
He's 8 months old.
-Aww.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.352
His name's Buddy Prine.
We love him.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:09.755
We named him after John Prine,
who we're huge fans of.

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:12.224
And, yeah --
It's funny, 'cause I was --

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:14.293
Not that I wasn't a baby person,
but when people --

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:17.430
When I would see newborns,
I was kind of like, "Yeah."

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.565
-Yeah. You're like,
"Okay, yeah, yeah, sure."

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:22.301
-And then when I had him, like,
I was truly convinced he was

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.704
actually the most beautiful baby
that had ever been born.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.572
To the point where I was
almost embarrassed

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.007
for us in the hospital.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:30.009
People would come in.
I'd be like, "It's insane.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:32.111
I know."

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.879
-"I know. It's insane." Yeah.

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.682
"We actually have the most --
yeah, the best-looking baby."

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:36.983
-And I look back on photos,
and I'm like,

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.184
"No, he was a newborn."

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.220
-He looked like a baby, yeah.
-He's awesome.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.121
-This is your first time
away from baby.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.656
-Yeah.
-How's it going?

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:47.159
Are you --
-I slept for 15 hours.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:49.562
-Yeah! That's what
I'm talking about! Really?

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.664
-This should be required
for new moms.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.966
Glam and 15 hours of sleep.

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:56.368
-And this. And you.
-Oh, good.

00:03:56.368 --> 00:03:59.304
-But also the sleep.

00:03:59.304 --> 00:04:01.507
-Obviously people know you
from "Search Party."

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.109
-Mm-hmm.
-Congrats on the great reviews.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:05.478
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:08.447
But now, here you are,
doing this new film,

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:10.449
"Vacation Friends"
with John Cena,

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:13.085
and it is the biggest
film opening --

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:14.754
original movie
in Hulu's history.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.556
So, not bad,
making a little history.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.124
-Thanks. Thanks.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.525
-It's a huge hit.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.593
-And I heard
that it's just announced

00:04:21.593 --> 00:04:23.428
that there might be
a sequel being made.

00:04:23.428 --> 00:04:26.733
-Yeah, we got a sequel,
which is so amazing, right?

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.167
Yeah.
-That's gigantic.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.838
-Thanks. I'm -- I'm geeked out.
-I mean, that's great.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:34.207
We know John and Lil Rel,
as well.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.641
-They're the best.

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:37.176
-They're just fun on set.
-Oh, unbelievable.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.111
Like, they're both
such comic geniuses.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:40.980
-But you're pretty
brilliant yourself.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.414
-Thanks, man.
-Can we set up what

00:04:42.414 --> 00:04:44.450
"Vacation Friends" is about?
-Yeah.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.919
It's a film about two couples
that are very --

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:50.055
They become very --
They're unlikely friends.

00:04:50.055 --> 00:04:52.024
John Cena and I play, like, the
couple you cannot get rid of,

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:53.759
that you meet for like five
minutes and you're like,

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:55.995
"They were nice," and then
you just can't lose them.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.697
-Yeah.
-But it's a really fun movie.

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.299
I think it's --
it's a good feel-good --

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:00.933
Reminds me of,
like, old-school comedies

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.335
in a way that's refreshing.
-Yeah.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.836
That's what we kind of want
right now.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.037
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:07.106
Here's Meredith Hagner
in "Vacation Friends."

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:09.241
Take a look at this.
-Get comfortable.

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:11.711
Oh, and if you guys are worried
about privacy and you want to,

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.213
like, get really kooky tonight,
we're extremely loud.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:16.048
I don't know what these walls
are made of,

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:18.651
but you seriously
can't hear anything!

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:19.952
Okay. Listen.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.487
[ Doors close ]

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.689
[ Screams ]

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:26.291
[ Doors open ]

00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:29.495
You're not gonna believe this.
I just screamed in there.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.297
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.365
-Meredith Hagner, everybody.

00:05:33.365 --> 00:05:35.067
"Vacation Friends"
is streaming now on Hulu.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.869
-Thanks, guys.
-Congratulations

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.504
on Baby Buddy Prine.
-Yeah.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.039
-I love that.
-Thank you.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:42.375
-Baby Keem performs for us
after the break.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.744
Stick around, everybody.
Thank you so much.

